hi there Steve Kaufman here so it's week  two our 12 week or 90 day challenge  today I want to talk about the  importance of varying your activities in  order that you don't get bogged down or  feel frustrated and one of the ways that  we keep track of your level of  activities of course is the coins the  coins are because you get coins for  different kinds of activities therefore  you want to be accumulating as many  coins is kind of an indicator a  milestone of how active you are and of  course the more active you are the  faster you're gonna learn but if you're  always doing the same thing it gets a  bit boring I once had a boss at work who  told me it's a long road that has no  curves we need a little bit of variety  and so you can vary the content and I  have spoken in the past about what I  call the short term activities which is  really working the basic structures of  the language and that's something that  is featured a lot in our mini stories  the most common phrases the most common  structures but on the other hand you  want to move forward into more difficult  authentic content where you are  acquiring more words and of course the  linking activity itself you can deal  with it in different ways one thing that  linking does is it enables you to look  up a word add it to your database you'll  come across that again it's highlighted  in yellow gradually gradually as you if  you review through flashcards you don't  have to do but it's another activity  that you can use you slowly move that to  where it becomes a part of your  initially passive vocabulary and  possibly active vocabulary so you need  to acquire these new yellow links but  even in content that you have already  studied and this is something I point  out in the workshop that I did  day you can go back into material that  you looked at three four five months ago  that you think you know you'll discover  there lo and behold there are words that  you thought you knew that you don't know  link them again don't feel concerned  about moving words to knowledge because  you're afraid you might forget them  again or that they will no longer be  known it doesn't matter you come across  them again you're not sure what they  mean you link them again another thing  that I find very useful when I go  through something for that tenth timing  is to create phrases because the phrase  is embody and the structure the grammar  of the language and the goal of course  is not to be trying to remember the  rules all the time but to find certain  phrasing natural and its natural its  meaning immediately and it just feels  natural that that's the way you say it  and if you read it and listen to it and  find it in different situations often  enough you will be able to produce that  as well so I think today in our second  week I want to emphasize that you should  vary your activities certainly do all  the different activities that are gonna  earn coins but also be flexible and  creative and how you use your links  don't worry too much about moving  something to know that you're gonna then  forget make sure you introduce enough  variety of activities enough variety of  content so the experience remains fresh  for you because the brain requires both  repetition and novelty so keep it new  keep it fresh very things be flexible  and don't get frustrated like as I today  I had a conversation in Arabic I  struggled mightily to speak in Arabic  probably worse than I did three weeks  ago and this is all going to be part of  your learning you'll do better some days  than other days and yet as long as you  stay  that you will over time improve that's  kind of what language learning is light  and the goal of eventually being humble  able to understand and connect with  different cultures and to communicate  makes it all worthwhile  so there you have it week two by canal
 

